  "plain": "In the 1950s, a US Air Force intelligence unit called the 4602nd Air Intelligence Service Squadron is said to have written in its own official history that part of its job was calming the public about UFOs. Michels quotes the document directly: the aim was \"reassuring the public mind that no tangible evidence existed to support the fears of an invasion from outer space.\" He brings it up because it suggests the unit's goal was reassurance, not just investigation."
